schema: concept-lineage
object:
  title: Onchain Donation Transparency
  type: concept-lineage
  short_description: >-
    Publishing blockchain-verifiable proof of how donated crypto funds are
    used — e.g. a nonprofit publishing its wallet address so donors can trace
    fund flows directly, without relying solely on the organization's own
    reporting.
  source_traditions:
    - traditional nonprofit financial-transparency/annual-reporting practice
    - blockchain's public-ledger property (any transaction is traceable by
      design)
    - crypto-philanthropy platforms and communities (the article's cited
      source, CryptoAltruists Web3 Impact Toolkit)
  toolkit_usage: >-
    Positioned in this article as a differentiator crypto donors specifically
    value, tied to the donor-motivation category "transparency" and offered as
    a concrete stewardship action nonprofits can take (publish a wallet
    address, share transaction IDs in thank-yous).
  adjacent_meanings:
    - onchain transparency as a technical property of any public blockchain
      (baseline, not donor-facing)
    - onchain transparency as a deliberate donor-relations practice (this
      article's framing — actively surfacing that traceability to donors)
  important_distinctions:
    - >-
      technically-traceable-vs-actively-communicated — a transaction being
      technically traceable on a public ledger is different from a nonprofit
      actively publishing and explaining that trace to donors; the article's
      recommendation is specifically about the latter, more deliberate
      practice.
  tensions:
    - >-
      donor-trust-benefit vs organizational-financial-privacy — publishing a
      wallet address exposes an organization's full transaction history
      (including amounts and counterparties) publicly and permanently, a
      trade-off this short article does not explore in depth.
  risks_of_flattening: >-
    Presenting onchain transparency as a purely additive trust-building
    feature flattens the real trade-off (permanent public exposure of an
    organization's full financial activity) that the article's brevity does
    not surface.
  maturity: raw
  ai_assisted: true
  provenance:
    origin: src/content/docs/donor-stewardship.md
    transformation: summarized
    authorship: ai-assisted
  work_order: wo-6040541f9808
